// FR3 Dynamic Model — Independent Sensor Simulation
// Metatron Dynamics, Inc.
//
// Computes joint torque from published FR3 inertial parameters.
// This is the independent physics path that replaces the V0.1.0
// tau_meas = F × L shortcut identified in Verifier finding V0.1.0-HOLD.
//
// Source: fr3_hand.urdf autogenerated from fr3.urdf.xacro
// Repository: frankarobotics/franka_description (Apache 2.0)
// Mirrored at: gitlab.cc-asp.fraunhofer.de/ipk_aut/converging/
//              impedance_controller (commit 68dcefc0)
//
// This computation uses:
//   1. Published link masses (kg)
//   2. Published link centers of mass (m, in link frame)
//   3. Published joint origins (m, rotation/translation between frames)
//   4. Declared configuration θ₁=0, θ₂=0
//   5. Declared external payload at end-effector
//
// It does NOT use F × L.
// It does NOT use the conventional treatment formula.
// It computes gravity torque by summing contributions of each
// link's weight acting at its center of mass, plus the payload.
//
// τ_gravity[joint] = Σ_i ( m_i × g × r_i_horizontal )
// where r_i_horizontal is the horizontal distance from the joint
// axis to the center of mass of link i, at the declared configuration.
//
// This is what a physics engine (Gazebo/MuJoCo) computes internally.
// We compute it directly from the published parameters.

use crate::fr3_geometry::G_M_S2;

